course: dictionary
lesson: 5081
title: Insults and how they hurt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An insult is a rude remark or action that hurts someone's feelings or shows no respect. To insult someone is to say or do that thing to them. Insult can be a noun or a verb: «an insult» names the thing, and «insulted» tells you what someone did.
explain: Context clues help you here. «The wise moves: ask, don't assume; discuss ideas, never insult people» sets insulting people against discussing ideas politely. Insulting is the opposite of respect, so this sentence tells you insult means something rude and unkind.
explain: Some insults use words that seem harmless. «"svynya" means pig; calling someone "svynya" is an insult meaning a pig or slob.» The word on its own is just an animal. It becomes an insult because of how it is used to hurt someone.
explain: Insults can make people feel awful. Ethan is picked on every day, and he lies awake thinking «Why me?» Name-calling is a kind of bullying, and it is never okay. If someone insults you, tell a trusted adult.
fact: An insult is a rude, unkind remark or action.
fact: To insult someone is to say or do something that hurts their feelings or shows no respect.
fact: «An insult to our intelligence» means something so bad it seems to show disrespect.
fact: Name-calling is a kind of bullying, and insults hurt.
fact: «Hurl insults» means to throw insults at someone, and «add insult to injury» means to make a bad thing worse.
exercise: «The wise moves say: never insult people.» What does insult mean here? | A question about the time | A song sung at a party | A kind word to a friend | *A rude, unkind remark or action
exercise: «"svynya" means pig; calling someone "svynya" is an insult.» What is "svynya"? | *A pig, used as an insult | A school subject | A type of food | A kind name for a friend
exercise: Find the verb form of insult in this sentence and copy it: «Ali insulted his brother after the game.» | after | *insulted | game | Ali
test: Calling someone names every day is a kind of what? | Rhyming | Sharing | Winning | *Bullying
test: When an insult makes a bad thing even worse, the phrase is: | Take it as a compliment | Hurl insults | *Add insult to injury | Trade insults
exam: Which statement about insults is correct? | *An insult is a rude remark that hurts someone's feelings | An insult is always a compliment | Insults are a kind of kind word | Insults only matter if you are a grown-up
